# Captain dev workflow (mandatory)

Read **`docs/agents/captain-dev-workflow.md`** for full detail. Every task follows:

**① Ticket → ② Lavish plan (captain approves) → ③ Build → ④ Review → ⑤ Promote**

## ① Ticket first (default)

If the captain describes work, a bug, an idea, or pastes feedback — run **workflow
plan** (ticket + Lavish) before anything else, even if they did not ask.

```bash
npm run workflow:plan -- --chat "<their message>"
```

Ticket only (no plan yet): `npm run linear:ticket -- --chat "…"`

Skip only when they explicitly say **"no ticket"**.

Reply with **PRP-###** + full Linear URL + plan path. **Stop until approved — build.**

See **`lavish-plan-gate.mdc`** and `docs/share/proplane-collaborator-workflow.md`.

## ② Plan in Lavish (before code)

**Do not implement** until the captain approves the plan. Phase ② is included in
`npm run workflow:plan` above; enrich the HTML and poll for feedback:

1. `npx -y lavish-axi poll .lavish/plans/PRP-###-…/plan.html`
2. UI work: follow `docs/agents/ui-change-checklist.md`

Skip only when they say **"skip plan"** (hotfix).

## ③ Build

- **Default:** commit on **this pane's keeper branch only** (`cursor-2` here — see
  `local-agent-branch.mdc`). Push to `origin/cursor-2`. No remote feature branches.
- **Experiments:** `scripts/proplane-test-branch.sh start <slug>` → work → `finish` or `abort`.
- Reference **PRP-###** in commits.
- Read `docs/agents/<area>.md` before coding.

## ④ Review

Test on **http://localhost:3011** (this sandbox). Update Linear. Hand off to captain —
do not merge to prakrit yourself.

## ⑤ Promote (captain only)

When captain says merge to **prakrit**:

```bash
bin/fm-proplane-promote-to-prakrit.sh cursor-2
```

That merges into integration and **resets all agent sandboxes** from `origin/prakrit`.
Captain verifies localhost:3000.

## Subagents

Paste phases ①–③ constraints into every subagent brief (security-review, bugbot, explore).

## Production data (never)

**Never read/write/update production** resident, property, task, lease, charge, or
message data. Dev/test Supabase only. See `no-production-data-writes.mdc`.
